.\" Clean-room re-authoring derived from the observed behavior of Apple's
.\" /usr/bin/pbpaste.  The prose lives in pbcopy.1, which documents both
.\" programs; .so is used here to share it, and ln(1) is the portable form.
.TH PBPASTE 1 "September 25, 2026" "LibreDarwin"
.SH NAME
\fBpbpaste\fR \- write the pasteboard to standard output
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pbpaste
writes the first available pasteboard item to standard output, choosing the
type as described in
.BR pbcopy (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pbcopy (1),
.BR open (1),
.BR textutil (1)
.BR tiffutil (1)
